  "description": "Flat dahlia-disk shells that bloom into layered rows of radial petals \u2014 warm coral cores fading to gold tips across concentric petal rings. Unlike spherical chrysanthemums, dahlia bursts spread in a wide flat disk before petals curl and fall. Bass expands disk radius, mids stagger petal-row timing, treble adds micro-petals. Mouse detonates a personal dahlia at the cursor. Aging rows hook into an involute curl, and a pistil disk of short florets sits inside the first row.",
